<comment> pushi (I-type, opcode 111001) removed: opcode reassigned to tanh by the activation engine </comment>
<comment> Activation engine instructions (project add-on, opcode prefix 111). Decoded by dlx_control: 1110xx = sigmoid block (opcode[1:0]: 00=sigmoid 01=tanh 10=gelu), 111100 = relu, 111101 = softmax. Syntax: sigmoid RD RS1 imm - the trailing imm must be written (use 0x0); the hardware ignores it. RESA parses 2-operand I-types as RS1,imm, so the full lw-style arg list is required. Actions for sigmoid/tanh/gelu are placeholders (RESA cannot model the Q16.16 hardware math); real results come from the FPGA. </comment>
<command>
<type>I</type>
<opcode>111000</opcode>
<name>sigmoid</name>
<function>000000</function>
<action>MR[RD]:=MR[RS1]</action>
<args>RD,RS1,imm</args>
<isbranch>false</isbranch>
</command>
